WEBVTT

00:00:59.839 --> 00:01:01.729
"Now, don't you think we need

00:01:01.729 --> 00:01:05.800
more than one black person in the U.S. Senate?"

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:07.828
Now Harold and I --

00:01:07.828 --> 00:01:10.346
(Applause) —

00:01:10.346 --> 00:01:13.435
we still laugh about that story,

00:01:13.435 --> 00:01:16.871
and in many ways, the moment caught me off guard,

00:01:16.871 --> 00:01:19.891
but deep, deep down inside,

00:01:19.891 --> 00:01:22.015
I actually wasn't surprised.

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:23.438
And I wasn't surprised because of something

00:01:23.438 --> 00:01:26.574
my mother taught me about 30 years before.

00:01:26.574 --> 00:01:29.989
You see, my mother was ruthlessly realistic.

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:31.981
I remember one day coming
home from a birthday party